# The pages this site used to publish about a player, at /player/<slug> and /players, are gone. A
# player has one URL now and it is the search page itself, so somebody arriving from a search engine
# lands in the tool rather than on a summary of it.
#
# 301 and not 410: the URLs are retired, not disowned. Everything they earned moves to the new one,
# and the links already out there keep working.
#
# The sitemap is redirected for a different reason: Google has it registered under the old name, and
# without this it would fall through to the catch-all below and be served the application's HTML -
# which reads as a broken sitemap rather than a moved one.
#
# These have to come first. The catch-all matches everything, and the first match wins.
/player/*            /search/opponent/:splat  301
/players             /search                  301
/sitemap-players.xml /sitemap-opponents.xml   301

# Every other path is a route of the single-page application, answered by its shell.
/*  /index.html  200
